<title>NORWAY: Oil output at Statoil's Heidrun back to normal.</title>
<headline>Oil output at Statoil's Heidrun back to normal.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil production at the Heidrun field in the Norwegian Sea off mid-Norway is back to normal output of 250,000 barrels per day (bpd), operator Den norske stats oljeselskap AS (Statoil) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The field had been operating at about 220,000 bpd due to water injection problems.</p>
<p>Heidrun was shut in for maintenance between September 2 and 12.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
